grep for generation|isCurrent|const g|gEntry inside lines 2098-2164 returns zero matches — confirmed no generation capture and no isCurrent() call anywhere in the function. Two awaits: createSection (line 2123) and assignMemberSection (line 2155). Both settle-time writes are unconditional: the tree mutation sections = insertSectionNode(sections, newNode, input.parentId) at line 2148 (after the first await, before the second) and sectionWriteError = {...} at lines 2108/2126/2160 (all three sites, none generation-checked). patchMemberSectionIds at 2163 is likewise unguarded. Matches issue #299's claim exactly: no guard of any kind.

